<Item XName="Text" Type="Param">
<DataEntry>Note:&#x000D;&#x000A;The FPGA designs and generated FPGA programming files of FPGA0 and FPGA1 are the same. But we can configure different FIR coefficents to the defined BlockRegisters in FPGA0 and FPGA1. Then we can bypass the calibration FIR filter for FPGA0 and compensate IQ imballance via FPGA1&apos;s calibration FIR filter.&#x000D;&#x000A;You can also use Register &quot;IsSrcFPGA&quot; and &quot;IsEndFPGA&quot; to dynamically configure FPGA0 and FPGA1.&#x000D;&#x000A;For FPGA0, IsSrcFPGA =1, IsEndFPGA = 0.&#x000D;&#x000A;For FPGA1, IsSrcFPGA =0, IsEndFPGA = 1.&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;If above picture can&apos;t be loaded in this schematic, please find and view &quot;multi-channel_cali_FPGA_arch.png&quot; in the same directory as this example workspace.</DataEntry>
<TextParam><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></TextParam></Item></Item>
